%% title: Balance Hold Lifecycle (Card Authorisation / Pending Transfer)
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> ACTIVE : POST /api/v1/balances/{accountId}/holds\n{amount, currency, reason, referenceId, expiresAt}\nreserved_amount += amount\navailable_amount -= amount

    ACTIVE --> RELEASED : DELETE /api/v1/balances/holds/{holdId}\n(authorisation expired / cancelled)\nreserved_amount -= amount\navailable_amount += amount

    ACTIVE --> CAPTURED : POST /api/v1/balances/holds/{holdId}/capture\n(card transaction settled)\nreserved_amount -= amount\npending_amount += amount

    ACTIVE --> AUTO_EXPIRED : expires_at reached\n(scheduled cleanup job)\nreserved_amount -= amount\navailable_amount += amount

    CAPTURED --> [*] : TransactionCommitted event consumed\npending_amount -= amount\nbooked_amount -= amount

    RELEASED --> [*]
    AUTO_EXPIRED --> [*]

    note right of ACTIVE
        Hold ID is the stable
        card-authorisation reference.
        Optimistic lock (version)
        prevents concurrent
        double-release.
    end note

    note right of CAPTURED
        pending_amount bridges
        the gap between
        authorisation and
        ledger settlement.
    end note
